  "method": "Two models, averaged with equal weight. Model 1 is our own simple model: inflation drifts back toward the RBA's 2.5% target (AR(1) mean reversion), and the cash rate moves part of the way each quarter toward a Taylor-type target of 3.5% neutral + 1.5 x (forecast inflation - 2.5%). Model 2 is TimesFM, Google's open-source pretrained forecasting model, run on the RBA history with no tuning. The central path is the average of the two (cash rate rounded to 0.05-point steps). The 80% band is deliberately wide: it runs from the lower of the two models' bands to the higher of their upper bands. Not an official forecast; use as a rough guide only.",
